  <h2>Read a post-launch review with evidence limits</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Greenline review file</h3>
    <p><b>Preparation:</b> The May 3 booking launch covered current desktop browsers and two current phone models. The written test plan did not include three older phone models that accounted for 18% of mobile visits during April. A compatibility warning for those models was present in the vendor documentation, but the project record does not show whether anyone had read that section before launch.</p>
    <p><b>Launch:</b> Between 9:00 a.m. and 1:45 p.m., 64 users on the three older models reached the final booking screen but could not save. At 1:50, the team requested vendor approval for rollback. Approval arrived at 2:18, and rollback finished at 2:30. The team restored 51 bookings from temporary server records; 13 users needed to submit their information again.</p>
    <p><b>Current effect:</b> At 10:00 the next morning, staff were still processing 29 duplicate or incomplete requests. The rollout plan had no offline form, and the support team had no approved process for importing a temporary spreadsheet.</p>
    <p><b>Review conclusion:</b> Testing the three older models might have revealed the compatibility problem, but the missing test cannot establish what the team would have noticed. A preapproved rollback could have reduced the approval wait. If the plan had included an offline form and import process, staff would probably have had a smaller backlog the next morning. The file supports adding those safeguards; it does not support assigning the entire outcome to one person.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You reconstructed the missing coverage, affected users, rollback opportunity, present backlog, and calibrated review conclusion from the complete file.">
    <h3>Evidence check: keep every counterfactual inside the record</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The plan omitted three older phone models that accounted for 18% of April mobile visits." data-hint="Combine the missing device group with its stated share of prior mobile visits." data-fix="The test plan omitted three older phone models accounting for 18% of April mobile visits."><p class="quiz-question">1. What documented preparation gap made an additional compatibility test relevant?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The plan omitted three older phone models that accounted for 18% of April mobile visits.">The plan omitted three older phone models that accounted for 18% of April mobile visits.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team tested every device used during April.">The team tested every device used during April.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The file contains no information about device coverage.">The file contains no information about device coverage.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Sixty-four users could not save; 51 bookings were restored, and 13 users had to resubmit." data-hint="Preserve all three launch counts and their different meanings." data-fix="64 users could not save, 51 bookings were restored, and 13 users needed to resubmit."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which summary accurately reports the affected bookings?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Sixty-four users could not save; 51 bookings were restored, and 13 users had to resubmit.">Sixty-four users could not save; 51 bookings were restored, and 13 users had to resubmit.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All 64 bookings were permanently lost with no recovery.">All 64 bookings were permanently lost with no recovery.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Only 13 users reached the final screen, and 51 never used it.">Only 13 users reached the final screen, and 51 never used it.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It could have removed or shortened the 28-minute approval wait, although the total rollback time is not established." data-hint="Compare the 1:50 request with the 2:18 approval and preserve what the file does not measure." data-fix="Preapproval could have reduced the 28-minute approval wait; the file does not establish the total time it would have saved."><p class="quiz-question">3. What opportunity could a preapproved rollback have created?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It could have removed or shortened the 28-minute approval wait, although the total rollback time is not established.">It could have removed or shortened the 28-minute approval wait, although the total rollback time is not established.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It would certainly have prevented every save problem before 9:00.">It would certainly have prevented every save problem before 9:00.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It would have changed the April device statistics.">It would have changed the April device statistics.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Staff were still processing 29 duplicate or incomplete requests at 10:00 the next morning." data-hint="Recover the exact present-effect count, type of work, and time." data-fix="At 10:00 the next morning, staff were processing 29 duplicate or incomplete requests."><p class="quiz-question">4. What present consequence forms the endpoint of the mixed-conditional analysis?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Staff were still processing 29 duplicate or incomplete requests at 10:00 the next morning.">Staff were still processing 29 duplicate or incomplete requests at 10:00 the next morning.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every booking had become complete before launch.">Every booking had become complete before launch.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The vendor was processing 190 new phone models.">The vendor was processing 190 new phone models.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Add older-device tests, preapproved rollback, an offline form, and an import process without assigning the whole outcome to one person." data-hint="Recover the four safeguards and the explicit responsibility boundary." data-fix="The file supports four safeguards and rejects assigning the entire outcome to one person."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which recommendation stays within the review evidence?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Add older-device tests, preapproved rollback, an offline form, and an import process without assigning the whole outcome to one person.">Add older-device tests, preapproved rollback, an offline form, and an import process without assigning the whole outcome to one person.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Claim one tester caused every failure and that one extra test would certainly have prevented all harm.">Claim one tester caused every failure and that one extra test would certainly have prevented all harm.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Remove every safeguard because a counterfactual can never inform planning.">Remove every safeguard because a counterfactual can never inform planning.</button></div></div>
