  <h2>Notice and repair the time relationship</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="would" data-hint="The standard unreal past if-clause needs had plus the participle known." data-fix="If we had known about the warning, we would have expanded the test." data-why="Use the Past Perfect in a standard Third Conditional if-clause; would have belongs in the alternative result here." data-success-message="Correct. Had known now marks the unreal past condition, while would have expanded remains in the result.">
    <h3>Repair 1: keep <span class="ex">would have</span> out of the standard past condition</h3><p>Tap the auxiliary with the wrong job.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="if">If we</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="would">would have known</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="warning">about the warning,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="expanded">we would have expanded the test.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="find" data-hint="After might have, use the past participle found." data-fix="The older-phone test might have found the problem before launch." data-why="A modal perfect result uses modal plus have plus past participle: might have found." data-success-message="Correct. Found now completes the modal-perfect chain for an uncertain past result.">
    <h3>Repair 2: supply the past participle</h3><p>Tap the base verb where a participle is required.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="test">The older-phone test</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="might">might have</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="find">find</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="launch">the problem before launch.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="have processed" data-hint="The sentence explicitly says staff are doing the work now, so use an ongoing present result." data-fix="If the plan had included an offline form, staff would not be processing the backlog now." data-why="The unreal condition belongs before launch, but the stated consequence is an activity happening now; would not be processing preserves that mixed time." data-success-message="Correct. The result now ends in the current ongoing backlog rather than an unreal completed past action.">
    <h3>Repair 3: preserve the present endpoint</h3><p>Tap the result phrase that puts the consequence at the wrong time.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="if">If the plan had included</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="form">an offline form,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="have processed">staff would not have processed</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="now">the backlog now.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Practice fair analysis without disclosing a real regret</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to discuss a real mistake, disciplinary action, missed opportunity, medical decision, financial loss, relationship, immigration choice, academic failure, or private workplace incident. Use Greenline, a tutor-created case, or a fictional project. The goal is precise time and evidence control, not personal confession or blame.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Timeline reconstruction:</b> State three known events in chronological order. Change one past condition and identify whether the consequence belongs in the past, present, or future.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Modal ladder:</b> Keep the same unreal condition. Give a <span class="ex">would have</span> result supported as expected, a <span class="ex">could have</span> opportunity, and a <span class="ex">might have</span> outcome that remains uncertain.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Evidence challenge:</b> Your partner asks, <span class="ex">What makes that consequence plausible?</span> Name the mechanism and evidence, weaken the modal, or withdraw the claim.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Register shift:</b> Give one neutral version with <span class="ex">if</span>. Then reformulate it once with selective formal inversion. Keep the time relationship and certainty unchanged.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: lead a 90-second counterfactual review</h3>
    <p>Use the Greenline file or another tutor-supplied fictional case. Reconstruct the actual timeline and identify one piece of information available at the time. Build one Third Conditional with a past result, one mixed conditional with a present or future result, and one mixed conditional in which a continuing characteristic affects a past result. Use <span class="ex">would, could</span>, and <span class="ex">might</span> for three genuinely different claims. Include one negative form and one question. Reformulate one sentence with conditional inversion. Name one uncertainty and one practical safeguard. When the reviewer challenges a causal link, defend it with evidence, weaken it, or withdraw it.</p>
    <p><b>Success criteria:</b> Can the listener recover the actual record, changed condition, condition time, consequence time, modal meaning, evidence, uncertainty, and recommended safeguard without hearing <span class="ex">if...would have</span> in the standard past condition, a broken auxiliary chain, a false certainty claim, or unsupported personal blame?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved counterfactual reality, time mapping, complete form, calibrated modal meaning, conditional inversion, evidence limits, and U.S. spoken form.">
    <h3>Final check: reconstruct and calibrate the alternative</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If the team had tested the older phones, it might have found the compatibility problem before launch." data-hint="Use the Past Perfect condition and might have plus participle for an uncertain past result." data-fix="If the team had tested the older phones, it might have found the compatibility problem before launch."><p class="quiz-question">1. The missing test may or may not have revealed the problem. Which Third Conditional preserves that uncertainty?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the team had tested the older phones, it might have found the compatibility problem before launch.">If the team had tested the older phones, it might have found the compatibility problem before launch.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the team would have test the phones, it definitely finds every problem.">If the team would have test the phones, it definitely finds every problem.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the team tests yesterday, the problem might found.">If the team tests yesterday, the problem might found.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If the plan had included an offline form, staff would have less backlog work now." data-hint="Put the missing safeguard in the unreal past and the workload consequence in the present." data-fix="If the plan had included an offline form, staff would have less backlog work now."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence connects a missing past safeguard to a present workload?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the plan had included an offline form, staff would have less backlog work now.">If the plan had included an offline form, staff would have less backlog work now.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the plan includes a form yesterday, staff had less work now.">If the plan includes a form yesterday, staff had less work now.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the plan would include a form, staff have processed tomorrow yesterday.">If the plan would include a form, staff have processed tomorrow yesterday.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If the approval process were faster, the team could have restored service sooner yesterday." data-hint="Use a continuing process characteristic in the condition and could have for a lost past opportunity." data-fix="If the approval process were faster, the team could have restored service sooner yesterday."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence connects an unreal continuing characteristic to a past opportunity?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the approval process were faster, the team could have restored service sooner yesterday.">If the approval process were faster, the team could have restored service sooner yesterday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the process had faster, the team could restored now yesterday.">If the process had faster, the team could restored now yesterday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the process will be fast, yesterday is restored.">If the process will be fast, yesterday is restored.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Had the team tested the older phones, it might have found the problem." data-hint="Remove if, invert had and the subject, and keep the participle tested." data-fix="Had the team tested the older phones, it might have found the problem."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which formal inversion preserves the original conditional meaning?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Had the team tested the older phones, it might have found the problem.">Had the team tested the older phones, it might have found the problem.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Had tested the team if the phones, it finds the problem.">Had tested the team if the phones, it finds the problem.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Would the team had tested, it might found the problem.">Would the team had tested, it might found the problem.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The missing test creates a plausible detection possibility, but the record does not prove detection or justify assigning the whole outcome to one person." data-hint="Preserve the usefulness of the counterfactual and both stated evidence limits." data-fix="The test might have detected the problem; the record proves neither detection nor individual responsibility for the whole outcome."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which interpretation stays inside the Greenline evidence?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The missing test creates a plausible detection possibility, but the record does not prove detection or justify assigning the whole outcome to one person.">The missing test creates a plausible detection possibility, but the record does not prove detection or justify assigning the whole outcome to one person.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The record proves that one tester’s attitude certainly caused every later problem.">The record proves that one tester’s attitude certainly caused every later problem.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because detection is uncertain, no future safeguard can be useful.">Because detection is uncertain, no future safeguard can be useful.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If we’d known contains had; we would’ve acted contains would have with weak have." data-hint="Use the participle after ’d to recover had, then expand would’ve as would have." data-fix="If we’d known means if we had known; we would’ve acted means we would have acted."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which explanation accurately expands <span class="ex">If we’d known, we would’ve acted</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If we’d known contains had; we would’ve acted contains would have with weak have.">If we’d known contains had; we would’ve acted contains would have with weak have.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both contractions mean would of in standard writing.">Both contractions mean would of in standard writing.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We’d known contains would before a base verb.">We’d known contains would before a base verb.</button></div></div>
