  <h2>Reflect: can you defend the changed relationship?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the counterfactual decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">The actual layer contains...</span> <span class="ex">The alternative layer changes...</span> <span class="ex">A Third Conditional keeps...</span> <span class="ex">A Mixed Conditional is needed when...</span> <span class="ex">Could have differs from might have because...</span> <span class="ex">Would have is not proof because...</span> <span class="ex">If we had known differs from if you would wait because...</span> <span class="ex">Had we known is...</span> <span class="ex">The next safeguard follows from...</span></p>
    <p>Then draw two short timelines for one fictional case. Put the actual events above the line and unreal alternatives below it. Mark each condition and result as past, present, or future. Add one evidence note and one uncertainty note before choosing the modal.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
